/**
* Gets or sets the {@link ClickInputMode} that is used by this instance to determine clicks.
* Whenever the mode detects a {@link ClickInputMode.addClickedListener click}, this mode will use the {@link IHitTester} from the {@link MultiplexingInputMode.inputModeContext} to determine the items being hit. If they match the
* {@link GraphInputMode.clickableItems} type, the {@link GraphInputMode.addItemClickedListener ItemClicked} event will be triggered. If
* they {@link GraphInputMode.shouldFocus}, the item will be {@link GraphInputMode.setCurrentItem set as the current item}.
*
* If no value has been set explicitly, the factory method {@link GraphInputMode.createClickInputMode} will be called
* upon first access. Upon change the {@link GraphInputMode.onClickInputModeChanged} method will be called.
*
* By default this input mode has a priority of `10`.
*
*
* __Disabling the ClickInputMode on its parent input mode__
* ```
* mode.clickInputMode.enabled = false
* ```
*
* [Read this documentation online](https://docs.yworks.com/yfileshtml/#/api/GraphInputMode%23clickInputMode).
*
* @throws {@link Exception} __(NotSupportedError)__ If an attempt is made to change the instance while this mode is {@link IInputMode.install installed}. To exchange a mode, first
* {@link IInputMode.uninstall}, then {@link IInputMode.install reinstall} to ensure that all data is initialized correctly.
* @see {@link GraphInputMode.onItemClicked}
*/
get clickInputMode(): ClickInputMode;
set clickInputMode(value: ClickInputMode);
