/**
Adds the given listener for the `QueryName` event that occurs when a name is queried.
This event can be used to override name mappings to XML names in XAML.

If the event handler determines that it map resolve {@link QueryNameEventArgs.type} to a xml name, it should place the result into the {@link QueryNameEventArgs.result} property and
thus mark the event as {@link QueryNameEventArgs.handled}.

It is valid to provide only part of the XML name by setting the other part to null. In that case, the default name
determination rules are used for that part.

@param listener The listener to add.
@see {@link GraphMLIOHandler.removeQueryNameListener}*/
addQueryNameListener(listener: (sender: this, evt: QueryNameEventArgs) => void): void;
/**
Removes the given listener for the `QueryName` event that occurs when a name is queried.
This event can be used to override name mappings to XML names in XAML.

If the event handler determines that it map resolve {@link QueryNameEventArgs.type} to a xml name, it should place the result into the {@link QueryNameEventArgs.result} property and
thus mark the event as {@link QueryNameEventArgs.handled}.

It is valid to provide only part of the XML name by setting the other part to null. In that case, the default name
determination rules are used for that part.

@param listener The listener to remove.
@see {@link GraphMLIOHandler.addQueryNameListener}*/
removeQueryNameListener(listener: (sender: this, evt: QueryNameEventArgs) => void): void;
