export enum CurveConnectionStyle {
/**
Curve connection style that keeps the port and the first/last segment that the layout algorithm would produce without
curve routing.
- For the {@link HierarchicLayout} the edge ports are distributed according to the specified {@link HierarchicLayoutNodeLayoutDescriptor.portAssignment} and the {@link HierarchicLayoutEdgeLayoutDescriptor.minimumFirstSegmentLength minimum first segment length}
as well as the {@link HierarchicLayoutEdgeLayoutDescriptor.minimumLastSegmentLength minimum last segment length} are considered. This way the edges keep the original hierarchic connection
style and the first/last segment remains orthogonal.
- For the {@link EdgeRouter} the edge ports are distributed as usual and the the {@link EdgeRouterEdgeLayoutDescriptor.minimumFirstSegmentLength minimum first segment length} as
well as the {@link EdgeRouterEdgeLayoutDescriptor.minimumLastSegmentLength minimum last segment length} are considered. This way the edges keep the original connection style and the
first/last segment remains orthogonal.
- For the {@link CurveRoutingStage} the edge ports as provided by the specified {@link LayoutStageBase.coreLayout core layout algorithm} are kept,
including the starting segment provided by it. The {@link CurveEdgeLayoutDescriptor.minimumFirstSegmentLength minimum first segment length} and the {@link CurveEdgeLayoutDescriptor.minimumLastSegmentLength minimum last segment length} is
considered if the core layout did consider it too.

@see {@link HierarchicLayoutRoutingStyle.sourceCurveConnectionStyle}
@see {@link HierarchicLayoutRoutingStyle.targetCurveConnectionStyle}
@see {@link EdgeRouterEdgeLayoutDescriptor.sourceCurveConnectionStyle}
@see {@link EdgeRouterEdgeLayoutDescriptor.targetCurveConnectionStyle}
@see {@link CurveEdgeLayoutDescriptor.sourceCurveConnectionStyle}
@see {@link CurveEdgeLayoutDescriptor.targetCurveConnectionStyle}*/
KEEP_PORT,
/**
Curve connection style that changes the part of a curved edge path such that the curves have a more organic-like and
straight start or end.
The port location is specifically amended for the curve routing such that the connecting part of the curve can be routed
directly into the required edge direction. This feature generates more direct and straighter routes that have less
direction turns. In consequence, the resulting layouts may be more compact overall as less space for the routing is
required.

The side where the port ends up at the source/target node may be changed with respect to the side the layout algorithm
initially chooses. It is not changed if there are port constraints defined for it (i.e. {@link PortConstraint}s or
{@link PortCandidate}s). This includes implicit constraints for the port due to port and edge grouping. Similarly,
this style can also not be applied if there is an edge label or
{@link NodeHalo}s that require the connecting segment to remain as it is.

In contrast to
{@link CurveConnectionStyle.KEEP_PORT}, this style does not guarantee to respect the specified minimum first and
last segment length settings.

@see {@link HierarchicLayoutRoutingStyle.sourceCurveConnectionStyle}
@see {@link HierarchicLayoutRoutingStyle.targetCurveConnectionStyle}
@see {@link EdgeRouterEdgeLayoutDescriptor.sourceCurveConnectionStyle}
@see {@link EdgeRouterEdgeLayoutDescriptor.targetCurveConnectionStyle}
@see {@link CurveEdgeLayoutDescriptor.sourceCurveConnectionStyle}
@see {@link CurveEdgeLayoutDescriptor.targetCurveConnectionStyle}*/
ORGANIC
}
