/**
Returns a {@link ILayerConstraintFactory} instance that can be used for specifying layer constraints for the
given graph.
The instance is usually bound to {@link Graph} instance
`graph`, i.e., if the input graph for the layerer changes, a new instance must be retrieved. This instance can be used for
creating constraints for this graph instance.

You can create an instance without binding it to a graph instance initially by passing a `null` parameter. In that case,
you __must__ bind the returned instance to the graph, see {@link HierarchicLayout.LAYER_CONSTRAINTS_MEMENTO_DP_KEY}
and {@link ILayerConstraintFactory.memento}.

__Warning:__ {@link ILayerConstraintFactory} instances have to be {@link ILayerConstraintFactory.dispose disposed} after use if a `graph` was passed in. Disposing
the factory will also remove all constraints previously specified for the factory's associated graph. Creating layering
constraints with a disposed factory will throw an {@link Exception InvalidOperationError}.

__Warning:__
Creating a new constraint factory for the given graph will render all previously created factories (including any
constraints specified) bound to that graph useless. Therefore, a new constraint factory should only be created after
previously used factories have been properly disposed.

[Read this documentation online](https://docs.yworks.com/yfileshtml/#/api/HierarchicLayout%23createLayerConstraintFactory(Graph)).

@param graph the input graph
@returns a new {@link ILayerConstraintFactory} instance*/
