/**
Gets or sets whether or not nodes should be placed in a more compact style with respect to layout width.
If enabled, the algorithm may place the nodes of a layer in a stacked style (horizontally interleaving), i.e., it splits
the layer into an upper and lower sublayer and places adjacent nodes into different sublayers if this reduces the width
of the layer.

## Note

Enabling this option increases the required layout height.

__Warning:__ This option does not work with customized {@link IDrawingDistanceCalculator}s, see {@link HierarchicLayoutCore.drawingDistanceCalculator}.

## Note

Nodes within a {@link HierarchicLayout.TABULAR_GROUPS_DP_KEY tabular group} are never placed in a stacked style.

[Read this documentation online](https://docs.yworks.com/yfileshtml/#/api/SimplexNodePlacer%23nodeCompaction).

@see {@link SimplexNodePlacer.minimumSublayerDistance}
@see {@link SimplexNodePlacer.assignNodesToSublayer}*/
get nodeCompaction(): boolean;
set nodeCompaction(value: boolean);
/**
Gets or sets the minimum distance between the upper and lower sublayer.
A too small distance value may prevent adjacent nodes from being placed in a stacked style (horizontally interleaving)
because the vertical distance between these nodes must be greater than or equal to the value specified by {@link HierarchicLayoutNodeLayoutDescriptor.minimumDistance}.

Values should be greater than `0`.

__Warning:__ This option is only considered if the node compaction {@link SimplexNodePlacer.nodeCompaction is enabled}.

@throws {@link Exception} __(ArgumentError)__ if minimum sublayer distance is negative
@see {@link SimplexNodePlacer.nodeCompaction}*/
get minimumSublayerDistance(): number;
set minimumSublayerDistance(value: number);
/**
Gets or sets whether or not the {@link SimplexNodePlacer} places labels in a more compact style.
If this option is enabled the algorithm tries to place adjacent label elements in a stacked style, i.e., horizontally
interleaving.

## Note

This option has no effect with customized {@link IDrawingDistanceCalculator}s, see {@link HierarchicLayoutCore.drawingDistanceCalculator}.*/
get labelCompaction(): boolean;
set labelCompaction(value: boolean);
/**
Gets or sets whether or not an optimization step should be applied that tries to further reduce the number of bends.
## Note

Using this option may increase the running time of the layout algorithm. If the running time exceeds the maximum
duration (see {@link SimplexNodePlacer.maximumDuration}) the number of bends is not reduced.

## Note

Disabling option {@link SimplexNodePlacer.barycenterMode} may further reduce the number of bends.

__Warning:__ The optimization is not applied in case that tabular group nodes are defined (see
{@link HierarchicLayout.TABULAR_GROUPS_DP_KEY}).

[Read this documentation online](https://docs.yworks.com/yfileshtml/#/api/SimplexNodePlacer%23bendReduction).

@see {@link SimplexNodePlacer.maximumDuration}*/
get bendReduction(): boolean;
set bendReduction(value: boolean);
/**
Gets or sets whether or not the {@link SimplexNodePlacer} tries to create a maximally compact horizontal
layout at the cost of more bends.
For best results, {@link SimplexNodePlacer.breakLongSegments} and {@link SimplexNodePlacer.labelCompaction} should also be enabled.

@see {@link SimplexNodePlacer.labelCompaction}
@see {@link SimplexNodePlacer.breakLongSegments}*/
get horizontalCompaction(): boolean;
set horizontalCompaction(value: boolean);
/**
Gets or sets whether or not a postprocessing step should be applied to reduce the number of bends.
Furthermore, enabling this option may violate some minimum distances specified by the user and the edge distribution is
no longer uniform.

## Note

This option is only considered if option {@link SimplexNodePlacer.nodeCompaction} is disabled.*/
get straightenEdges(): boolean;
set straightenEdges(value: boolean);
/**
Gets or sets the strategy used for controlling the horizontal compactness of group nodes.
## Note

To obtain compact groups you should additionally disable option {@link SimplexNodePlacer.bendReduction}.*/
get groupCompactionStrategy(): GroupCompactionPolicy;
set groupCompactionStrategy(value: GroupCompactionPolicy);
/**
Gets or sets whether or not the {@link SimplexNodePlacer} enforces the placement of nodes at their exact
current positions, even if this violates minimum distance constraints.*/
get exactPlacement(): boolean;
set exactPlacement(value: boolean);
/**
Gets or sets whether or not the {@link SimplexNodePlacer} should try to use the coordinates given from the
current sketch for the determination of the layer coordinates.*/
get fromSketchLayerAssignment(): boolean;
set fromSketchLayerAssignment(value: boolean);
/**
Gets or sets the time limit (in milliseconds) set for the layout algorithm.
Values have to be greater than or equal to `0`.

## Note

Restricting the maximum duration may result in a lower layout quality. Furthermore, the real runtime may exceed the
maximum duration since the layout algorithm still has to find a valid solution.

@throws {@link Exception} __(ArgumentError)__ if the maximum duration is negative*/
get maximumDuration(): number;
set maximumDuration(value: number);
