/**
The {@link OrganicLayoutConstraintFactory} allows to define additional constraints on subsets of a graph that
will be applied by the {@link OrganicLayout} during the layout calculation.
Constraints modify the behavior of the organic layout algorithm for subsets of a graph, in order to introduce
structures, relative positioning, or area restrictions on the positions of the nodes in the layout.

The constraints are defined on IDs registered to the nodes with a {@link IDataProvider} with the key
{@link LayoutKeys.NODE_ID_DP_KEY}

A {@link OrganicLayoutConstraintFactory} has to be {@link OrganicLayoutConstraintFactory.dispose disposed of} after use. Disposing of the factory will also
remove all constraints previously specified for the factory's associated graph.

__Warning:__ For grouped graphs, any one constraint may only be applied to nodes with the same parent.

__Warning:__ Contradictory constraints may be violated. If the scope of the organic layout is not set to {@link OrganicLayoutScope.ALL} or
{@link OrganicLayout.nodeOverlapsAllowed overlaps are not allowed}, the specified constraints may be broken in favor of the other features if it is necessary.

__Warning:__ Some features of the {@link OrganicLayout} can contradict the constraints specified here. In that case,
conflicts are resolved as follows:

- If the graph is {@link PartitionGrid partitioned}, constraints that are not compatible with the partition grid can be broken.
- If a partial layout is applied to {@link OrganicLayout.chainSubstructureStyle chains}, {@link OrganicLayout.cycleSubstructureStyle cycles}, {@link OrganicLayout.starSubstructureStyle stars}, {@link OrganicLayout.treeSubstructureStyle trees}, {@link OrganicLayout.parallelSubstructureStyle parallel structures} or
{@link OrganicLayout.groupSubstructureScope groups}, constraints that include the affected nodes will be ignored.
- If the graph contains
{@link OrganicLayout.scope fixed nodes}, those nodes will remain fixed. Constraints affecting those nodes will be enforced if possible, which may
decrease the quality of the resulting layout. If the constraints are impossible to enforce without moving the fixed
nodes, they can break.
- An {@link OrganicLayout.EDGE_ORIENTATION_DP_KEY edge orientation} that contradicts constraints specified here, may lead to undefined behaviour w.r.t. the orientation
of the edge and the affected constraints.

[Read this documentation online](https://docs.yworks.com/yfileshtml/#/api/OrganicLayoutConstraintFactory).*/
